    LLM: 'Game: 52 Pick-up. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: '52 Pick-up is a social prank using a standard pack: one player offers a game, scatters the cards, and the other player is left to pick them up. It is recorded as a social card-game joke rather than a strategic contest.',
    objective: 'As a group, score as many correct guesses as possible from the thirteen-card deck.',
    gameplay: 'The guesser draws a word card and chooses a numbered word without seeing it. Other players secretly write one-word clues. Identical or too-similar clues are removed before the guesser sees the remaining clues and makes one guess, passes, or misses.',
